---
const benches = [
  {
    name: 'The terminal',
    kicker: 'Software & ML',
    blurb: 'Data pipelines, machine-learning models, and the APIs that serve them.',
    tools: [
      'Python',
      'Scikit-learn',
      'FastAPI',
      'Supabase',
      'JavaScript',
      'Git',
      'AI-assisted design',
    ],
    icon: '<rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="m7 9 3 3-3 3M13 15h4"/>',
  },
  {
    name: 'The garage',
    kicker: 'Electrical & mechanical',
    blurb: 'Electrical systems and engines, built with real safety margins.',
    tools: [
      'DC electrical design',
      'PWM speed control',
      'Thermal management',
      'Safety systems',
      'Engine rebuilding',
      'Diagnostics',
    ],
    icon: '<path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/>',
  },
  {
    name: 'The floor',
    kicker: 'Operations',
    blurb: 'Workflows that move faster without trading away safety.',
    tools: [
      'Six Sigma',
      'Lean',
      'Process mapping',
      'KPI design',
      'Team leadership',
      'Change management',
    ],
    icon: '<rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7" rx="1"/><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7" rx="1"/><path d="M10 6.5h4.5a3 3 0 0 1 3 3V14"/><path d="m15 11.5 2.5 2.5 2.5-2.5"/>',
  },
];
---

<section
  id="about"
  aria-labelledby="about-title"
  class="border-y border-line bg-page-alt py-section md:py-section-lg"
>
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>03 — About</p>
        <h2
          id="about-title"
          class="mt-6 font-display text-display-xl font-medium [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_144]"
          data-reveal
          style="--reveal-delay: 80"
        >
          Systems thinking, with grease under <em>the fingernails.</em>
        </h2>
        <div
          class="mt-10 max-w-prose space-y-6 text-body-lg"
          data-reveal
          style="--reveal-delay: 160"
        >
          <p>
            For more than fifteen years I’ve solved operational problems at one of Michigan’s
            largest distribution centers — the kind of place where one inefficient process ripples
            out to fifty-plus store routes. It taught me to see work as a system: find the
            bottleneck, fix the flow, measure the result.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            That way of thinking followed me home. It’s why I taught myself Python and machine
            learning, why I rewired my son’s ride-on for 24 volts, and why I tore an ATV engine down
            to the last component instead of just fixing what broke.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="lg:col-span-5 lg:pt-28" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240">
        <figure class="card relative p-8 sm:p-10">
          <svg
            class="h-10 w-10 text-accent"
            viewBox="0 0 40 40"
            fill="currentColor"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path
              d="M17 10c-6 2.2-10 7.4-10 14.2V30h10V20h-5.4c.5-3.6 2.8-6.3 6.6-7.7L17 10Zm16 0c-6 2.2-10 7.4-10 14.2V30h10V20h-5.4c.5-3.6 2.8-6.3 6.6-7.7L33 10Z"
            ></path>
          </svg>
          <blockquote
            class="mt-6 font-display text-heading-lg font-normal italic leading-snug [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_72]"
          >
            I treat AI as a sophisticated thinking partner, not a replacement for engineering
            judgment.
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="mt-6 text-muted">
            It’s a force multiplier — it accelerates learning, improves design quality, and helps me
            tackle problems I couldn’t solve alone, from designing FishCast’s ML architecture to
            debugging complex, multi-layered technical issues.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-20 md:mt-28">
      <h3 class="eyebrow font-mono" data-reveal>The toolbox — three workbenches</h3>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          benches.map((bench, i) => (
            <li
              class="bench card flex flex-col p-7 sm:p-8"
              data-spotlight
              data-reveal
              style={`--reveal-delay: ${i * 110}`}
            >
              <span class="inline-flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-line text-accent-ink">
                <svg
                  class="h-5 w-5"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  fill="none"
                  stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.75"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  set:html={bench.icon}
                />
              </span>
              <p class="mono-label mt-8">{bench.kicker}</p>
              <p class="mt-2 font-display text-heading-lg font-medium">{bench.name}</p>
              <p class="mt-3 text-muted">{bench.blurb}</p>
              <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2 pt-2">
                {bench.tools.map((tool) => (
                  <li class="chip">{tool}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .bench {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.4s ease;
  }
  .bench:hover {
    border-color: rgb(var(--accent) / 0.5);
  }
  .bench::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    background: radial-gradient(
      26rem circle at var(--mx, 50%) var(--my, 0%),
      rgb(var(--accent) / 0.13),
      transparent 60%
    );
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.4s ease;
  }
  .bench:hover::before {
    opacity: 1;
  }
</style>
